[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-41839"] :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=xyz\\,i+{e}^{-y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x\\,j+({e}^{-y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi z+2xz)\\,k.$ \nEvaluate $∇\\cdot F$ at the point $(1,0,0).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{-y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({e}^{-y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi z+2xz) \\\\  & =yz-{e}^{-y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi x+\\pi {e}^{-y}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi z+2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(1,0,0),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\cdot F)(1,0,0) & =(0)(0)-{e}^{0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +\\pi {e}^{0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+2(1) \\\\  & =0-(-1)+\\pi (1)+2 \\\\  & =1+\\pi +2 \\\\  & =\\pi +3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-105573/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "6694ff0b-ce44-5267-940f-03bc7eaa739d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105573/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "f472db3d-2365-5ac8-aabd-622d96e4a11a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105573/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "5eecea38-b79a-5b54-9dd2-2616c15784b2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105573/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "d5cd3210-ff40-58f5-a265-8951fd4a2f9e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105573/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" :answer/id #uuid "04614be6-49ef-5da8-8cb7-8d07bfe2629f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105573/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d260d722-a004-5ffb-8989-3c47ec75d87d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105573/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-105573/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" "q-105573/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-105573/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-105573/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-105573/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105573" :question/id #uuid "cb71e2f3-58c2-5fe5-b7fd-919a06f927d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-105573" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060047/assets/3088d088689bbd0dfd33abe8240c6f02cceb257937fc1fccb8ba3df151dbfaab.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\n- $\\text{div}\\,F=0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F>0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F<0$\n- $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060047/assets/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement II is true, whereas statements I and III are false. Notice that the lengths of the vector's $y$-components increase as we move vertically away from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the vector field $F$ acts like a source at every point.\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0,$ the vector field $F$ is not solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105573/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105573"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105576/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "e7589e4d-9501-5cb7-a8be-6a05142e9723" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105576/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" :answer/id #uuid "93b3d037-d808-54ef-a3a5-b7d76867a9b7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105576/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" :answer/id #uuid "2e511b20-f647-5935-b693-8f0e6e7ff1f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105576/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "a173872e-2039-5f10-be0a-23d2a52c4a34" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105576/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "ef1f6cee-c0e4-5688-91d5-b3fd28fbb35b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105576/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "664359e7-76a5-5834-98f5-947262b90783" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105576/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer-field/choices ["q-105576/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" "q-105576/selection/48ed73fa8fff01bdc324b4f21abd0bd25d38fe050f7a804787ee07e14c349dd0" "q-105576/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" "q-105576/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-105576/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105576" :question/id #uuid "1a9b7bd5-4597-5a75-b03e-038a1e45c570" :question/math-academy-id "q-105576" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060047/assets/cf932f4f02a216d5111da0748cb04f815a7d2e85af5db2f9282f5aefc359b816.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\n- $∇\\cdot F=0$\n- $∇\\cdot F>0$\n- $∇\\cdot F<0$\n- $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060047/assets/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statements II and III are false. For any point $P,$ the sum of the inward-pointing vectors equals the sum of the outward-pointing vectors. Therefore, $F$ acts neither like a source nor a sink.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere, the vector field $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105576/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105576"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123200/selection/ea469f3e53b818ab5b703dc09f193c7093ac0666865c0a5b323c43d7b199b090" :answer/id #uuid "6e5073d6-9aac-5387-ac87-532b3b27db45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "144" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123200/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7" :answer/id #uuid "63efa5e9-7250-5e71-9cbd-b4667d2d7ce6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "96" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123200/selection/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer/id #uuid "a076a420-51a8-57e9-bea4-675a98b5ff2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123200/selection/842947b00d8ffc5745884eed061ea57d57affe318d15d13be5c3612b41e13326" :answer/id #uuid "30613d7b-1211-51e8-a015-8b7f4b5597e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "84" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123200/selection/7ba4ebd0d8a414ae4c404538d01dce67a31f8f6714da9cff2a89b3a7ecb90e95" :answer/id #uuid "2ec0cfae-efb5-578f-9a25-ccb00c9e91fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "76" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123200/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "43fd2ca8-4514-54e8-917a-8e0bba17222f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123200/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7" :answer-field/choices ["q-123200/selection/ea469f3e53b818ab5b703dc09f193c7093ac0666865c0a5b323c43d7b199b090" "q-123200/selection/bc787d823ec953ec5e44b8f7f4a4c7f3b5de4a6a5f1cea9c5a660d6b5e6faac7" "q-123200/selection/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" "q-123200/selection/842947b00d8ffc5745884eed061ea57d57affe318d15d13be5c3612b41e13326" "q-123200/selection/7ba4ebd0d8a414ae4c404538d01dce67a31f8f6714da9cff2a89b3a7ecb90e95"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123200" :question/id #uuid "aa5cdcb7-c1f3-500e-aa56-d1ffbcb0b240" :question/math-academy-id "q-123200" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=(x-y)^{3}\\,i+(y+z)^{3}\\,j+(x+z)^{3}\\,k.$ Evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(-2,2,2).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j+R\\,k$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}+\\frac{∂R}{∂z} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x-y)^{3})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}((y+z)^{3})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}((x+z)^{3}) \\\\  & =3(x-y)^{2}+3(y+z)^{2}+3(x+z)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we evaluate $\\text{div}\\,F$ at the point $(-2,2,2),$ and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F(-2,2,2) & =3((-2)-(2))^{2}+3((2)+(2))^{2}+3((-2)+(2))^{2} \\\\  & =3(-4)^{2}+3(4)^{2}+3(0)^{2} \\\\  & =96.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123200/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6b79409-5a5b-533b-8d46-4e0e6d963b3a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123200"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-131193/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer/id #uuid "d4ad2e67-a50c-596a-8987-67f6f8d1c7db" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131193/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" :answer/id #uuid "fbf5550f-33c6-5bdb-bbd9-cd1571f04de8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131193/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "9125efa4-484c-51e4-a471-b8f823ef7c23" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131193/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "f4bb5d06-a6a3-5460-9aa5-02bfdb993f37" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131193/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "9784d2fc-9a09-5586-98e9-8eee5ac0ee6b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131193/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4374a794-c5c6-53a0-a9b2-53769b244d79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131193/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" :answer-field/choices ["q-131193/selection/0aba8feb8e80d6993512d064e058711be97ecf2a5cf7dd862ab928425f31c38c" "q-131193/selection/b733e7a470ea14913327e50fae585d7231209b41e08de1ba47b5dbb3c5f7d7d6" "q-131193/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-131193/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-131193/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131193" :question/id #uuid "f93fb39f-f5ac-593f-a746-5f36aa40a31a" :question/math-academy-id "q-131193" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060047/assets/243496443c3878c90fb67888add6c6ad6d3e69aa20ba24f42ee89d58a2742534.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true everywhere in the domain of $F?$\n\n- $\\text{div}\\,F=0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F>0$\n- $\\text{div}\\,F<0$\n- $F$ is solenoidal" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F$ denotes the divergence of the vector field $F.$\n\nIntuitively, the divergence of $F$ at a point $P$ measures how much $F$ acts like a source or a sink at $P:$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a source at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F>0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F<0$ at $P.$\n\n- If $F$ acts like neither a source nor a sink at $P,$ then $∇\\cdot F=0$ at $P.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14060047/assets/6c747149618d4c5ef35e727af15cd001365bd9c2d5e064689baf24c6ee23cff9.png)\n\nIf $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere in the domain of $F,$ we say that $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is true, whereas statements II and III are false. For any point $P,$ the sum of the inward-pointing vectors equals the sum of the outward-pointing vectors. Therefore, $F$ acts neither like a source nor a sink.\n\n- Statement IV is true. Since $∇\\cdot F=0$ everywhere, the vector field $F$ is solenoidal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and IV only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131193/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f47e201-105a-579a-8cde-fcb6bf8cfa2a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131193"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
